--------------------Below are the assert statements corresponding to all comments starting with "@@@" in the provided C# code:

1. Debug.Assert(OLD(x) + y = x) - This statement checks that the value of `x` increases by `y` after being passed into the function `Sum(int x, int y)`.

2. Debug.Assert(index >= 0 && index <= _size) - This statement ensures that the index is within the allowed range to insert an element in the `Insert(int index, Object value)` method.

3. Debug.Assert(_items, index, _size - index, _items, index + 1, _size - index) - It checks if the items are copied correctly into the ArrayList while inserting a new element.

4. Debug.Assert(index < 0 || index > _size) throw new ArgumentOutOfRangeException("nameof(index)", "SR.ArgumentOutOfRange_ArrayListInsert"); - It ensures that the 'index' is a valid index to remove an element at the index in the `Insert(index)` method.

5. Debug.Assert(_size == _items.Length) - It validates that the ArrayList is appropriately resized when the capacity is reached. Also, it checks the capacity was appropriately reset if the list is resized.

6. Debug.Assert(index - 1 >= 0 || index < _size - 1) - This ensures that the index being sought is within the range of list size.

7. Debug.Assert(((Array)_items).GetLowerBound(0) >= 0) - This ensures the lower-bound of array is always zero.

8. Debug.Assert(((Array)_items).GetUpperBound(0) <= _size - 1) - It checks if the List size maintains properly.

9. Debug.Assert(Array.IndexOf((Array)_items, value, 0, _size) >= 0) - It checks if given element is present in the list or not at the first occurrence.

10. Debug.Assert(LastIndexOf(value, _size - 1, _size) >= 0) - It checks last occurrence of a given element in the ArrayList.

11. Debug.Assert(index >= 0 && index < _size) throw new ArgumentOutOfRangeException("nameof(index)", "SR.ArgumentOutOfRange_Index"); - It checks if index is not out of bounds in RemoveAt method.

12. Debug.Assert(((Array)_items, index, _size - index, _items, index + 1, _size - index) != ((Array)_items).GetLowerBound(0)) - It checks if copy operation in Insert method is successful.

13. Debug.Assert(Array.IndexOf((Array)_items, value, 0, _size) >= 0) - This checks if the given element is present in the ArrayList or not, at first occurrence.

14. Debug.Assert(index < 0 || index > _size) throw new ArgumentOutOfRangeException("nameof(index)", "SR.ArgumentOutOfRange_Index") - It ensures that index lies within the range of possible for removal operation.

15. Debug.Assert(Array.IndexOf((Array)_items, obj, 0, _size) >= 0) - This ensures that object to be removed is present in the ArrayList.

16. Debug.Assert(index - 1 >= 0 || index >= _size - 1) - It makes sure that the 'index' has a valid range.

17. Debug.Assert(((Array)_items).GetLowerBound(0) >= 0) - It verifies the lower bound of the ArrayList is zero.

18. Debug.Assert(((Array)_items).GetUpperBound(0) <= _size - 1) - It ensures that the ArrayList maintains its size properly.

